# Shorts punch-first standard (locked)

**Do not upload, schedule, or leave public any Short ≥40 seconds.** Target **~20–28s** (sweet spot ~22–26s).

## Why

Retention evidence (2026-08): ~43s setup-led stayed ~27%; ~22s punch-first stayed ~67%. Growth is retention, not catalogue padding.

## Diamond bar (locked)

Winner pattern: *We Found Planets Made of Diamond* / live Three Suns remake (`MDvAKtmKauw`). Full auditor gate: `orbit-auditor-ship-gate.mdc`.

**Intensity (Orbit-adapted):** DECLARE 0–1s → ASSESS (one hard fact) → REVEAL last 4s + loop (highest peak). Never stretch to 60s / 6 Street Dog phases; no long PROCESS valley. Details in `orbit-auditor-ship-gate.mdc`.

1. Strange picture in **1s** — not Orbit, not a title card.
2. **Loop:** first ~3s and last ~4s are the same window (no mid-word seam).
3. **Captions** the whole Short — no holes.
4. **Thursday film title** on screen (~9–14s).
5. Length **22–27s** (never ≥40s).
6. End CTA on screen: “watch the full film →”; description = film title + parent long URL only; **zero `/go/`**.

## Build rules

1. **Punch-first open** — strongest fact / question in 0–1.5s (captions reinforce the punch).
2. **One idea** — curiosity-gap end; soft CTA last ~3s only.
3. **Exact parent long** — description link + Studio Related + **pinned** `Full film — {title}: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v={ID}` (zero `/go/`). Watcher: `npm run youtube:shorts-fullfilm`.
4. Prefer builders named `*_punch_*_v03.py` / `*_punch_*_v01.py` over legacy 40–45s launch cuts.

## Covers (locked 25 Aug 2026 — detail in `orbit-title-thumb-formula.mdc`)

1. **Scene-first 1080x1920** (9:16, <2 MB): one focal object + punch text ≤4 words, auto-fit to width.
2. **Never grab a fixed-% frame.** Score every frame (Orbit-orange, caption band, top-band busyness, brightness, detail): `tools/build_scene_first_short_covers.py`.
3. Short Orbit-dominated end to end → cover from the **parent film**, centre 9:16 crop, distinct beat per Short: `tools/build_covers_from_parent_episode.py`.
4. Upload covers via **Studio desktop only** (`tools/upload_shorts_covers_studio.py`) — the Data API letterboxes to 16:9 and never fills the vertical cover slot. Studio caps custom-thumbnail changes per ~24h; don't burn the quota with bulk API writes.
5. **Do not recut a Short to remove Orbit** — measured 25 Aug: Orbit-led median 47 views vs scenery-led 20.5 (r=+0.09). Scene-first is a cover rule, not a content rule.

## Replace rule (YouTube cannot swap files on an ID)

1. Upload new private punch cut → metadata/thumb parity.
2. **Scheduled:** set new `publishAt` exactly → unschedule old (private, no `publishAt`). Do **not** delete.
3. **Public:** make new public → privatize old. Do **not** delete.
4. Update registry / `SHORTS_UPLOAD_INDEX` / protected schedule lists; put old IDs in `historicalDuplicateIds`.

## Before any Shorts upload

- Probe duration; **abort if ≥40s**.
- Do not re-introduce superseded ≥40s IDs as canonical.
- Audit artifact for the 2026-08-12 rebuild: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/audits/shorts_40s_rebuild_2026-08-12/FINAL_40S_REBUILD_REPORT.md`.
